.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_STORE_GET0_PARAM 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_STORE_get0_param ,
.Nm X509_STORE_set1_param ,
.Nm X509_STORE_get1_objects ,
.Nm X509_STORE_get0_objects ,
.Nm X509_STORE_get1_all_certs
.Nd X509_STORE setter and getter functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509_vfy.h
.Ft X509_VERIFY_PARAM *
.Fo X509_STORE_get0_param
.Fa "const X509_STORE *xs"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_STORE_set1_param
.Fa "X509_STORE *xs"
.Fa "const X509_VERIFY_PARAM *pm"
.Fc
.Bd -literal
 STACK_OF(X509_OBJECT) *X509_STORE_get1_objects(X509_STORE *xs);
 STACK_OF(X509_OBJECT) *X509_STORE_get0_objects(const X509_STORE *xs);
 STACK_OF(X509) *X509_STORE_get1_all_certs(X509_STORE *xs);
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_STORE_set1_param
sets the verification parameters to
.Fa pm
for
.Fa xs .
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_get0_param
retrieves an internal pointer to the verification parameters for
.Fa xs .
The returned pointer must not be freed by the calling application
.Pp
.Xr X509_STORE_get1_objects 3
returns a snapshot of all objects in the store's X509 cache.
The cache contains
.Sy X509
and
.Sy X509_CRL
objects.
The caller is responsible for freeing the returned list.
.Pp
.Xr X509_STORE_get0_objects 3
retrieves an internal pointer to the store's X509 object cache.
The cache contains
.Sy X509
and
.Sy X509_CRL
objects.
The returned pointer must not be freed by the calling application.
If the store is shared across multiple threads, it is not safe to use
the result of this function.
Use
.Xr X509_STORE_get1_objects 3
instead, which avoids this problem.
.Pp
.Xr X509_STORE_get1_all_certs 3
returns a list of all certificates in the store.
The caller is responsible for freeing the returned list.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_STORE_get0_param
returns a pointer to an
.Vt X509_VERIFY_PARAM
structure.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set1_param
returns 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Pp
.Xr X509_STORE_get1_objects 3
returns a pointer to a stack of the retrieved objects on success, else
NULL.
.Pp
.Xr X509_STORE_get0_objects 3
returns a pointer to a stack of
.Sy X509_OBJECT .
.Pp
.Xr X509_STORE_get1_all_certs 3
returns a pointer to a stack of the retrieved certificates on success,
else NULL.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr X509_STORE_new 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Sy X509_STORE_get0_param
and
.Sy X509_STORE_get0_objects
were added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
.Sy X509_STORE_get1_certs
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Sy X509_STORE_get1_objects
was added in OpenSSL 3.3.
